## Model Routing Policy (owner's standing rule, 2026-09-17)

Three tiers, every tier at **HIGH effort**.

- **Fable 5.1 [1M]**: planning, design, architecture, context-inference reasoning → agent `architect-planner`
- **Opus 5 [1M]**: context governance (canonical and memory files, creating/editing/fixing skills and hooks) → agent `governance-worker`
- **Sonnet 5 [1M]**: code, scripts, implementation, inter-session communication and everything else. It is the session default (`"model": "sonnet"` in `~/.claude/settings.json`), so it needs no dispatch.

**Mechanism.** The two agent definitions carry `model:` + `effort: high` in their frontmatter. Dispatch with
the `Agent` tool: `subagent_type: "architect-planner"` / `"governance-worker"`; the tool's `model` param
overrides per call. Approval-board reviewers (every role, CEO included) go to `architect-planner`, never
inline. A skill cannot switch models: it is prose loaded into the running model, so the only lever inside
a skill is an explicit dispatch.

**Limit.** The base session model cannot be switched mid-session by any rule, skill or hook. Routing applies
only to dispatched subagents; running a whole session on Fable or Opus is a human choice at launch
(`/model`, `--model`).

