## Server-Only Automation (owner's standing rule, 2026-09-06; amended 2026-10-10)

Recurring work (every monitor, cron, routine, self-check and data-heavy research job) runs **outside the
user's PC and outside any open session**, and notifies the user by itself. The **mechanism of record** is
one of:

- the project's **remote server**, when it has one. Research compute runs niced with a memory cap so live
  services are never starved;
- a **cloud routine** (an Anthropic Routine), when the project has no server or the job is about repositories
  and PRs.

You talk to the loop or routine, not to a running agent: its prompt is self-contained, reads state from the
canonical files, keeps the same safety stops as a session (Verification Gate, Human-in-the-Loop, no
destructive action, no secret in the prompt) and reports through the notification channel. Session-bound
mechanisms (Monitor, CronCreate, `/loop`) are at most a convenience while a session is open, never the
mechanism of record. Every such change is written into the repo and the governance docs (CLAUDE.md,
HANDOFF, OPEN-PROBLEMS), not only announced in chat. Details: Agent Guide §18.3.

